\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {41}{\ignorespaces This plot illustrates the average value of production by age, across a variety of different metrics, smoothed by a LOESS estimator. Note that some of these estimates do not respect aging beliefs (i.e some metrics indicate infinite improvement with respect to age, as well as a decrease then improvement). This observation can be explained by selection bias; players who are more successful are likely to play later in their careers, and tend to have higher values of production, biasing curves upwards. }}{88}{figure.caption.81}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:empirical_production}{{41}{88}{This plot illustrates the average value of production by age, across a variety of different metrics, smoothed by a LOESS estimator. Note that some of these estimates do not respect aging beliefs (i.e some metrics indicate infinite improvement with respect to age, as well as a decrease then improvement). This observation can be explained by selection bias; players who are more successful are likely to play later in their careers, and tend to have higher values of production, biasing curves upwards}{figure.caption.81}{}}
